stage: decode (panic-class)
kind: panic — attempt to add with overflow
site: src/decode.rs:1038 (parse_class_data direct_methods loop, `method_idx_acc += diff`)
repro: cargo fuzz run fuzz_cfg fuzz/crashes/fuzz_cfg/panic-437a5b34bb53.bin
size: 1055 bytes

Surfaced during `dex-resource-limits` 15-minute libFuzzer gate on fuzz_cfg
(~2.29M runs in, ~6 minutes). `parse_class_data` in src/decode.rs has four
accumulator loops that decode field_idx_diff / method_idx_diff via ULEB128
and add them into `field_idx_acc` / `method_idx_acc` using `+=`. When a DEX
mutant supplies a large uleb delta, the u32 accumulator overflows and Rust
debug/release-with-overflow-checks aborts the process.

Four sites, all in `parse_class_data`:
  - src/decode.rs:987 (static_fields: field_idx_acc += diff)
  - src/decode.rs:1004 (instance_fields: field_idx_acc += diff)
  - src/decode.rs:1038 (direct_methods: method_idx_acc += diff) ← this crasher
  - src/decode.rs:1055 (virtual_methods: method_idx_acc += diff)

Fix: convert all four to `checked_add` and return `DexError::InvalidInstruction`
(or a new `DexError::IdxAccOverflow`). This is panic-class, not amplification;
per the `dex-resource-limits` brief it is explicitly out-of-scope and belongs
to `dex-hardening-sweep-2`.

Unblocks: the 15-minute libFuzzer gate on fuzz_cfg + fuzz_ssa without
`-fork=1`. With amplification bounded, this is the next (and, at least over
6 minutes, only) panic class sitting between the current state and "fuzz_cfg
and fuzz_ssa run 15 minutes clean".
